    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48081" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thălīa</span></b>  (written <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thălēa</span></b> , acc. to
			<i><span class="en">Fest.
			p. 359</span></i> Müll., and <i><span class="en">Serv. Verg.
			E. 6, 2</span></i>; so Rib.), ae, f., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Θάλεια.</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>One of the Muses; the Muse of Comedy</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. E. 6,
			2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. A. A. 1, 264</span></i>; <i>of
				Lyric poetry</i>, <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 4, 6,
			25</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>One of the Graces</i>, <i><span class="en">Sen.
				Ben. 1, 3, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">1, 3, 10</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A sea-nymph</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 5,
				826</span></i>.</div>
